WEBVTT

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.380
This place is Ryouzanpaku,

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.420
a gathering of martial arts masters.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:26.810
Sakaki Shio

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.990
Hundredth-degree black belt karate master,

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.600
Sakaki Shio.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.320
But they’re pretty good, ya know.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.460
Even though it was just a child’s fight.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:45.090
Ma Kensei

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.570
Lewd master of Chinese Kenpo,

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.200
Ma Kensei.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.620
That’s right. Ragnarok, was it?

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.770
Even though they’re just kids, they did manage to defeat the leader of Ragnarok.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:03.730
Apachai Hopachai

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.860
The Death God of Muay Thai,

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.640
Apachai Hopachai.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.700
When I hear “child’s fight”...

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.590
When I hear “child’s fight,” I feel sorry for the enemy.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.010
‘Cause he was fighting with all his strength and still lost.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.400
It's better not to call it a “child’s fight”.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.510
That’s... right.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:29.770
Kousaka Shigure

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.070
Master of swords and weapons,

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.770
Kousaka Shigure.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.000
Kenichi has no talent, but he tries so hard...

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.500
I’m not sure whether to admire him or...

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.000
Now, now, everyone...

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.160
don’t talk like that about him.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:50.250
Kouetsuji Akisame

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.000
Philosophical Jujutsu master,

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.040
Kouetsuji Akisame

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:54.000
...At least wait until he’s left the room.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:58.550
I can’t take it anymore!

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:06.250
Shirahama Kenichi

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.520
Shirahama Kenichi.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.230
A former bullied child...

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.550
currently in training to overcome his weaknesses.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.100
Don’t worry, man.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.020
He can’t hear us.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:20.570
Fuurinji Hayato

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.440
The oldest member of Ryouzanpaku,

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.670
"The Invincible Superman", Fuurinji Hayato.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:26.930
Oh my, that's another interesting machine I see there, Akisame-kun.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:34.350
Yes, it is a machine aimed to train one’s push,

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:37.270
pull, and psychological sharpness.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:42.790
I call it, “Take three steps forward or one step back is Hell.”

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.920
And, if he happens to lose his balance for just a moment...

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.150
the pulleys at the back will zap him into a disciplined shape with electrical shock.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.410
The electricity for this is generated by Kenichi’s exercise, so the power is provided for free!

00:02:55.410 --> 00:03:00.830
Woah! Akisame-kun, your inventions have brought you the rank of "master".

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.640
By the way, Ken-chan, does your body feel okay now?

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.920
Oh my, my words reached your ears.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:16.380
Well, uou certainly have come a long way, Ken-chan.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.850
Squeeeeeze

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.070
To think that you used to be a bullied child...

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:22.850
You murderer!

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.170
You murderer!

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.890
Gehhh!

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:29.330
Bear!!

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.910
Bear!!

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:33.360
but now you are the leader of Ragnarock, an esteemed group of delinquents...

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.410
and you defeated your childhood nemesis, Ryuuto-kun.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.260
Anyway, you mustn’t rest if you want to continue improving.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:43.900
You’re totally right!

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.500
And actually, you see, my...

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.010
It’s healed.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.790
Um, actually here and there it really...

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.840
You have developed very fine muscles.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:57.910
If Akisame-kun says so, I suppose you’re okay.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.330
You and Master think you know more about my body than I do. I hate you!

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.710
Let’s leave that for now...

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:09.530
Everyone, will you please gather?

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.990
We will now begin a Ryouzanpaku Strategy Meeting.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.380
Yami has begun to move.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:25.060
Ogata Isshinsai...

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:28.460
He is presently regaining powers...

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.530
and has declared war.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.760
It appears as though he has already joined forces with Yami.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:38.880
As you all know, he has appeared before Kenichi-kun.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.770
He was supposed to be a disciple here at Ryouzanpaku,

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.320
but he turned out to be a big mess.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.140
Good grief.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.050
It looks like he needs a good thrashing.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.680
Damn you, Ogata...

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:58.310
We had sworn to never pledge allegiance to Yami.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:01.700
If they do attack us as I predict,

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:06.810
then our strongest disciple will be in danger.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.880
Ohhh, but why’s that?

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.410
They wish to obtain the strongest warriors.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:15.470
And now that they know that Ryouzanpaku has a strong disciple...

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:19.120
we might as well consider them a personal threat.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:22.030
Kenichi-san is in danger?

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:29.170
Fuurinji Miu

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.550
Wings that cut through the wind,

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.270
the granddaughter of Ryouzanpaku,

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:28.660
Fuurinjin Miu.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.090
Wise one, have you any specific plans to conclude this meeting?

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:40.640
Yeah... Let us go with the usual plan.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.970
Heh, <i>that</i> plan, eh?

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.090
Yes.

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:48.460
Operation “Just Wing It”!

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.900
...I wouldn’t exactly call that a “plan”.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.510
Eavesdropping is a bad habit, my dear.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:04.530
Ken

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:04.530
Su

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.530
i

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.530
b

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:04.530
ch

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:04.530
DE

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.530
i

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.530
SU

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:12.010
Kenichi

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:12.010
SubDESU

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:12.010
The Strongest Disciple

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:12.010
Presents

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:17.500
A New Swordmaster

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:49.110
An opening!

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.900
How very impressive!

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:04.740
You deflected all the attacks not with simple blocking, but with additional counterattacks!

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:10.070
That is our method at Zanshin Taisha-ryuu. It is Shamyo no Ri.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:14.060
Rather than simply block, we use the inertia of an enemy’s attack against him.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.240
It is a trick that turns the tables.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.510
Those two have great form.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:25.050
Yes. Those two are our strongest disciples.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:30.740
I hope that they will represent our Zanshin Taisha-ryuu methods well and do you a good service.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.450
You two down there, what are your names?

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:36.580
We are pawns of Zanshin Taisha-ryuu.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.320
Names are not necessary.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:45.570
But if that’s the case, when you defeat Ryouzanpaku’s disciples...

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:50.160
and become one of us what will we call you?

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.690
Right, guys?

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.570
<i>Ah, good morning!</i>

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:09.490
Feels like it’s been forever since I’ve been in school!

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.040
I guess it couldn’t be helped.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:16.070
I was so injured that I couldn’t set foot outside Ryouzanpaku for a while.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.570
What the hell did you make this medicine out of?!

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.380
Glad to hear you’re well enough to scream.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:25.690
What are you doing there?

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.540
If you’re late for class you’ll be in even greater danger of flunking out.

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.220
C-Coming!

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:41.580
Okay, so in today’s lecture we’re going over some stuff you probably already know.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.450
Japanese history

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.460
Ken

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.460
’ichi

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.460
-san’s

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.460
notes

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.460
<Japanese history>

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.460
Miu-chan made it!

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:44.290
This will definitely be on the test...

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.040
Come, let’s go.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:00.210
Everyone has been worried about you, Kenichi-san!

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:02.730
I see.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.730
So everyone in the Shinpaku Alliance really cares about me.

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.930
Physics Lab

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.930
Shinpaku Alliance

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.930
headquarters

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:12.170
Niijima Haruo

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:10.840
Oh, it’s Kenichi-kun...

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:12.620
Didn’t you die or something?

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.120
You ass!

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.400
There, there...

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:20.600
Without you here, Shinpaku was proceeding so well!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.160
Well, if there’s any grunt work we’ll let you know.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:24.690
Gimme a freaking break!

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:27.100
Do you have any idea what hell I’ve been thr—

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.660
Long time no seeee!

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.130
Takeda-san! Ukita-san!

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:40.050
Flag: Shinpaku Alliance

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:35.470
That’s right. It looks like you’re perfectly healed.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:38.230
Hey, I thought you had broken bones.

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:40.050
You’ve got the regeneration powers of a monster.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:44.000
Well, he’s so lame he doesn’t even deserve to die.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.140
Niijima may be saying horrible things like that,

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:50.050
but honestly, he was VERY worried about you.

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:51.870
That's a lie...

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.810
That’s gotta be a lie.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:57.030
Huh? Where’s Tanimoto-kun?

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.190
Being a lone wolf as ususal.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.560
Try the roof.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:02.760
Tsk.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:05.690
So you survived, jackass?

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.300
Hey, man, don’t be so cold.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.300
You’re makin’ me cry!

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:11.730
There, there...

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:15.240
If you came here to ask about Odin...

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.790
Even I don’t know.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:21.480
Rumor is that Kensei took him away after you defeated him.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:23.320
I see...

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:26.280
His gang, Ragnarok, got disbanded...

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:29.260
I suppose there’s no way of finding him now even if I wanted to.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:32.220
Kenichi, your body is all healed, right?

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:34.400
Yes. Thanks for asking...

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:39.620
What the hell was that for?!

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:41.610
You need more training.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:46.520
Those aliens in Shinpaku don’t understand a goddamn thing.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:52.220
They had no idea that defeating Ragnarok would call forth an even scarier adversary.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.420
That paranoid ass!

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:05.510
I’m not gonna let him get to meee.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.440
I’ll just forget about it.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:11.640
Ahhhhh, caring for flowers sure soothes the soul.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:13.500
Kenichi-san.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.520
Ah, Miu-san.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:15.760
Are you off to rhythmic gymnastics?

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:28.230
Wh-What was that for?

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:29.810
I thought so...

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:31.130
It was a dead hit.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:36.250
Tanimoto-san would have dodged that attack!

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.730
That’s crazy talk!

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:41.030
Kenichi-san, you have become stronger.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:46.700
But if someone comes to kill you, someone with nothing to lose,

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.020
will you be able to fight back without holding back?

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:52.220
In ancient times,

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:57.440
it was said that if a fighter was attacked, his heart had to be constantly prepared to counter.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:02.200
Miyamoto Musashi, according to the tales, hated showing any sign of vulnerability.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.410
He never even took a bath.

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:06.110
Kenichi-san...

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:09.890
you have <i>not</i> prepared your heart to become a true fighter!

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.240
No way!

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:13.670
Hey, Fuurinji.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:15.600
We’re starting practice, with or without you.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:20.270
Jeez, I sure wish people would be punctual.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:21.480
Ms. Ace.

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:28.010
Takajima Chihiro

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.150
Takashima Chihiro. Like her last name, she’s a bit snobby.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:25.590
She used to be the star of the gymnastics club.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:28.050
She is bitter that her spot has been stolen from her.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.370
I understand.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.310
Let’s go, Chihiro-san.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:38.170
What’s his deal?

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:38.900
Not sure.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.130
I know I said some pretty harsh things,

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:46.010
but it's all for Kenichi’s sake, for his strength.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:50.780
But I wonder if he’ll be able to overcome the dangers of which my grandfather and the others spoke?

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:52.680
Miu-san...

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:57.690
You have <i>not</i> prepared your heart to become a true fighter!

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:09.780
Maybe that was just... coming from someone so well trained like Miu...

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:13.050
That was probably the worst thing I could have been told as a fighter.

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:16.930
Aw man. This means that the little bit of closeness our hearts had gained...

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:16.850
Sneak~

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.010
Flinch!

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:21.290
...has suddenly been destroyed in one fell swoop!

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.250
Whoosh!

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.640
This won’t do!

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:34.390
What’s wrong? You don’t look happy.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.380
Not really. It’s nothing.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:43.810
If you want the short answer, I just feel pathetic going shopping with my little sister at my age.

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:45.580
How can you say that, Onii-sama!

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:49.670
Accompanying his little sister while shopping is one of the sacred privileges a boy has!

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:50.880
Yeah, whatever.

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.810
Sorry, she never shuts up.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.400
Miu-san...

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:58.160
I don’t mind. In fact, I love a talkative shopping trip.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:07.690
Don’t walk so close to my brother!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.900
Well... you don’t need to walk <i>that</i> far from him.

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.990
I’m in a generous mood today.

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:19.710
Ohhh, you’re so cute! You’re so cute!

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.960
I’ve always wanted a little sister like you!

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.490
In that case, you can have her.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:26.980
Onii-chan!

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.770
Just kidding, just kidding.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:33.110
How peaceful.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:37.270
From grade school all the way to the third year of middle school, I was bullied the entire nine years.

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:41.510
Then when I learned martial arts, fighting became my life.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:46.830
That means that this time right now might be the happiest part of my life so far.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.670
I’d like to say that, but...

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:54.600
Tanimoto-kun and Miu-san are both telling me things are going to get even more dangerous.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:58.260
And if <i>they</i> say that, then things really must be dangerous.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.100
What kind of “danger” is waiting for me, though?

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:04.600
Ahhh, this won’t do.

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:06.390
Now I’m actually feeling scared.

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:11.820
Fine! It’s times like this that I must rely on the fighting manual by Daigakkan...

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:13.840
What are you reading?

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.050
Err, nothing!

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:19.130
Sign: Matsue Street

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:21.350
Ta-dah!

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.020
What do you think?

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.830
It’s so cute!

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:26.450
Anija{*old term for brother}, please!

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:26.450
TL Note: Anija is an old term for brother

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.020
Why <i>me</i>?

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:32.700
Buying clothes for his little sister is one of the many benefits of being a boy!

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:36.360
Mrrg... Buy it, buy it!

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:38.010
Fine, I will.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.110
Thank you very much.

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:54.020
What’s wrong, Miu-san?

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.060
Didn’t you notice?

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.880
Eh? Notice what?

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.430
The smell of a fight.

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:03.400
Yes, specifically the smell of blood lust.

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:17.630
What are those two people?

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:19.300
They feel almost like...

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:22.020
But I don’t know them.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:30.170
You got it!

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:32.070
What are you doing?

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:33.620
What’s going on?

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:37.350
So this is it... this is the danger?

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.470
This is the danger?!

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:41.540
Calm down, Kenichi-san.

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.350
Don’t get too excited.

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:47.900
She’s strong!

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.410
I mean, this doesn’t even seem possible!

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:52.780
I need to stay calm and block it...

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:59.130
Pathetic form. And you call yourself a man of Ryouzanpaku?

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.000
Who the hell are you two?!

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:08.000
Zanshin Taisha-ryuu pawn duo.

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:10.960
We pledge our lives to our cause.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.490
What did they say?! Their lives?!

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:14.210
Pawns?

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.080
What do you mean, “pawns”?

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:17.660
We ask the questions, not you!

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:19.990
Kenichi-san, you take on the man.

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:20.830
Okay!

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:25.220
Idiot. If he could barely stand up to me do you honestly think he stands a chance against my partner?

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:28.110
Kenichi-san can’t hit a lady!

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.250
His naivety will be his downfall!

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.440
How dare you destroy my favorite dress!

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.790
You’re not bad... for a target.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.100
I’m impressed, granddaughter of Ryouzanpaku.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:02.890
What?

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:03.690
What?

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:04.960
What?!

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.480
What a strong defense...

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.310
He’s strong...!

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:13.000
So this is the top fighter at Ryouzanpaku?

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:14.500
What’s your name, by the way?

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:17.080
Those who are prepared to die tomorrow need no names!

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.960
That’s fancy talk coming from someone who doesn’t know his own name!

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:22.080
Stop it, you idiot!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:26.520
How dare you bully my brother?! Damn you!!

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:29.590
You are not my assassination target.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.670
Impossible! How did he repel my fist?

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:45.760
Are you okay?!

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:47.440
Just fine, bro!

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:52.240
Stay back!

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:03.490
That boy... he’s almost like a different person.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:08.590
When one fights to protect that which he loves, his true power is released.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:12.160
For better or worse, this is the true Kenichi-san.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.460
Onii-chan! The train! The train!

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:21.340
I’m impressed, granddaughter or Ryouzanpaku.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.450
You’re not bad.

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:26.240
However, your beloved Ryouzanpaku ends tonight.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:28.290
What do you mean?

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:33.580
Yami ordered two of us to distract two of Ryouzanpaku’s strongest disciples.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.620
This was only a diversion.

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:43.500
Meanwhile, our strongest warriors are on their way to Ryouzanpaku to destroy the lot of them!

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.500
Wh-What did you say?!

00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:56.270
On this most glorious of days,

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:59.220
we, with Zanshin Taisho-ryuu, will claim this land as ours!

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:25.830
Beer always tastes best at sunset.

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:34.650
But when that happened, the fisherman must have thought...

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:39.800
Even for a TV in a dojo, you’re just too old!

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:42.860
Hmmm, how can a guy watch his DVDs in peace?

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.130
Charge!!

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:52.480
Onii-chan, watch out!

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:59.080
We've waited long for this moment... when you have no weapons.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.180
Prepare to die, Ms. Weapons-master!

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:05.730
...But I do have weapons.

00:21:08.380 --> 00:21:10.730
Your weapons belong to me...

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.600
and my weapons also belong to me.

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:21.700
Go warm yourselves up.

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:29.600
How dare you interrupt my beer time?!

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.340
I’ve only had one sip. How dare you?!

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.130
I wish you wouldn’t interrupt me.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:46.010
And so, if the two sides are tied together, the universe is bound as one.

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:49.980
Well? I’d like to ask your opinion on the matter.

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:52.020
K-Kill me!

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:02.070
I had no idea that such power existed...

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:07.270
But even if we are defeated,

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:12.140
right about now, your disciples are being destroyed by ours!

00:22:18.010 --> 00:22:19.110
Well, I’m not sure.

00:22:19.420 --> 00:22:21.470
I wonder if you’re right?

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:23.570
Onii-chan!

00:22:30.770 --> 00:22:32.470
Is he not afraid of death?

00:22:32.970 --> 00:22:34.940
What is that light deep in his eyes?

00:22:39.310 --> 00:22:40.600
I don’t recognize this move!

00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:43.630
If it isn’t an attack... then what is it?

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:45.520
Aim for the small point...

00:22:57.780 --> 00:22:59.530
Aren't you worried about your dojo?

00:22:59.530 --> 00:23:00.950
No, what I am worried about is...

00:23:01.790 --> 00:23:03.140
the condition of your partner!

00:23:06.890 --> 00:23:08.830
Fuurinji Big Wave!

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:14.810
Tsukasa!

00:23:17.270 --> 00:23:20.100
Well, there. You <i>do</i> have names.

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:25.420
As long as you have a gentle heart that can call out the name of someone you love, you can’t call yourself a pawn.

00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:41.350
If you ever have problems where you are, feel free to come to...

00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:43.660
Ryouzanpaku anytime.

00:23:43.970 --> 00:23:46.450
She’s right. I know they’ll help you out.

00:23:46.760 --> 00:23:51.080
Yes, even though you attacked their disciples...

00:23:52.010 --> 00:23:54.150
My name is... Kurando.

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:55.780
Yakabe Kurando.

00:23:56.440 --> 00:23:59.220
Ryouzanpaku disciples, what are your names?

00:23:59.610 --> 00:24:01.740
Kenichi. Shirahama Kenichi.

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:03.740
And I’m Honoka, his little sister.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:04.670
I see.

00:24:05.280 --> 00:24:06.180
What nice names.

00:24:11.900 --> 00:24:14.240
I hope those two will be okay...

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:19.350
Don’t worry about others, worry more about yourself.

00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:22.360
I will strive hard to be more serious next time!

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:27.450
Did I say something strange?

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:30.280
Not really.

00:24:32.310 --> 00:24:34.120
Now that just makes me even more curious!

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:37.690
Onii-chan, you’re targeted by bullies again!

00:24:37.690 --> 00:24:39.310
I’m worried about you.

00:24:39.310 --> 00:24:41.310
Wait up, Miu-san!

00:24:42.470 --> 00:24:46.150
Kenichi-san, you really are a unique fighter.

00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:49.000
I’m back!

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:51.030
We’re both back.

00:24:52.050 --> 00:24:53.790
Ah, they’re back.

00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:57.380
We don’t want to worry them with news of the attack, so keep it a secret.

00:24:57.830 --> 00:24:59.270
Where is... the enemy?

00:24:59.270 --> 00:25:01.650
Oh, we had them all carried away.

00:25:02.890 --> 00:25:04.680
That’s all, folks!

00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:08.270
Oh, hey there, you kids.

00:25:08.270 --> 00:25:10.550
<i>Nothing</i> happened while you were gone.

00:25:11.460 --> 00:25:13.040
Oh, is that s-so...

00:25:14.960 --> 00:25:20.960
But I see scratch marks on the walls... and half the roof looks burnt off...

00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:23.590
What the hell happened here?

00:25:24.770 --> 00:25:28.380
Miu-san, should we tell them about the pair that attacked us?

00:25:28.690 --> 00:25:30.960
We don’t want to worry them...

00:25:31.400 --> 00:25:33.240
and we made it out alive.

00:25:33.470 --> 00:25:34.760
Let’s keep it a secret.

00:25:34.760 --> 00:25:35.960
Good idea.

00:25:35.960 --> 00:25:39.470
Well, it was just the most <i>normal</i> day a person could have.

00:25:39.470 --> 00:25:43.010
Well, anyway, I think it’s time to make dinner.

00:25:44.850 --> 00:25:45.710
I’ll help you!

00:25:46.170 --> 00:25:49.640
Oh boy, I love a good dinner!

00:25:50.180 --> 00:25:53.940
Ken-chan, when dinner is over, go back to training.

00:25:53.940 --> 00:25:55.910
I’m wiped... out.

00:26:19.390 --> 00:26:25.780
Mado o tsutau ame sora wa tozasarete

00:26:19.390 --> 00:26:25.780
Rain falls down the windows from the closed sky.

00:26:19.390 --> 00:26:25.780
窓を伝う雨 空は閉ざされて

00:26:26.450 --> 00:26:32.950
Fui ni kodoku ni tsukamaru hi mo aru

00:26:26.450 --> 00:26:32.950
There are days when loneliness suddenly catches me.

00:26:26.450 --> 00:26:32.950
ふいに孤独に 捕まる日もある

00:26:33.960 --> 00:26:40.570
Kiyou demo nai shi chikamichi de wa nai

00:26:33.960 --> 00:26:40.570
I’m not very skilled, and I’m not on the easiest path.

00:26:33.960 --> 00:26:40.570
器用でもないし、近道ではない

00:26:40.990 --> 00:26:47.420
Dakara koso deaeta hito ga ita yo

00:26:40.990 --> 00:26:47.420
But that’s why I’m especially happy that I met you.

00:26:40.990 --> 00:26:47.420
だからこそ出逢えた人がいたよ

00:26:48.290 --> 00:26:54.860
Itsumo massugu na hitomi de itai yo

00:26:48.290 --> 00:26:54.860
I want your honest eyes to penetrate me always

00:26:48.290 --> 00:26:54.860
いつも真っ直ぐな瞳でいたいよ

00:26:55.740 --> 00:27:02.030
Negai hitotsubu, nagareteku

00:26:55.740 --> 00:27:02.030
My one wish shoots into the sky.

00:26:55.740 --> 00:27:02.030
願いひとつぶ、流れてく

00:27:02.630 --> 00:27:06.020
Staring eyes miteite ne

00:27:02.630 --> 00:27:06.020
Staring eyes, keep looking at me.

00:27:02.630 --> 00:27:06.020
Staring eyes 見ていてね

00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:09.680
Kitto kanaete miseru

00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:09.680
And I will make your wishes come true.

00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:09.680
きっと叶えてみせる

00:27:09.740 --> 00:27:14.150
Kasanaru koe to kodou, kanjite iru yo

00:27:09.740 --> 00:27:14.150
I feel our voices and heartbeats match up

00:27:09.740 --> 00:27:14.150
重なる声と鼓動、感じているよ

00:27:14.340 --> 00:27:17.310
Nakitaku naru toki mo

00:27:14.340 --> 00:27:17.310
Even in times when I want to cry.

00:27:14.340 --> 00:27:17.310
泣きたくなる時も

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:20.580
I just feel, “Thank you for you”

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:20.580
I just feel, “Thank you for you”

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:20.580
I just feel, “Thank you for you”

00:27:20.770 --> 00:27:24.160
Chiisa na boku no senaka ni

00:27:20.770 --> 00:27:24.160
Against my small back,

00:27:20.770 --> 00:27:24.160
小さな僕の背中に

00:27:24.280 --> 00:27:28.400
Kimi ga kureta yuuki, hane ni natte ku

00:27:24.280 --> 00:27:28.400
The courage you gave me turns to wings.

00:27:24.280 --> 00:27:28.400
君がくれた勇気、羽になってく

00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:31.000
“Hitori ja nai”

00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:31.000
“You’re not alone”

00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:31.000
「独りじゃない」

00:27:31.420 --> 00:27:35.920
My glory days

00:27:31.420 --> 00:27:35.920
My glory days.

00:27:31.420 --> 00:27:35.920
My glory days
